# Meeting room booking (test task)

**Goal:** UI to book a **meeting room** within one **work day (09:00–18:00)**. Authoritative spec: [`task.md`](../../task.md). If ambiguous — **ask**; do not guess silently.

## User capabilities (task.md)

- Select **date**
- View **existing bookings** for that date
- Choose **start** and **end** time
- **Create**, **edit**, **delete** booking
- **Display** (pick one): list, timeline, slot grid, or day calendar

## What reviewers expect (task.md)

- Solid **business logic** and **validation**
- UI states: **loading**, **empty**, **error**, **form submitting**
- **Server errors**, including **409 conflicts**
- **API layer separate from UI**, easy to swap for a real backend
- **Readable TypeScript** and clear **code structure**
- **Responsive** layout and basic **accessibility**
- **Engineering quality** over visual design

## Stack (task.md)

- **Next.js App Router** + **TypeScript** (task also allows React / Vue — this repo uses Next)
- Styles, state, forms — **your choice**; UI libs and icons **allowed**
- **No** real backend, auth, DB, or integrations — **mock API** only (Route Handlers + in-memory store; **MSW** etc. OK if UI uses `bookings-client` only)

## Timebox (task.md)

**4–6 hours.** If you stop early: README must say what you would finish and **priorities**.

## Deliverables (task.md)

- Link to **repository**
- **README:** how to run; what is done / not done; **time spent**; if incomplete — next steps and priorities
- **Deployed demo** (Vercel, Netlify, …)
- **AI chat** transcript

## Suggested layout

```text
app/page.tsx  app/api/bookings/  app/api/bookings/[id]/
lib/bookings/  lib/api/bookings-client.ts  components/bookings/
```

Domain rules **1–8:** [`booking-domain.mdc`](./booking-domain.mdc). API contract: [`bookings-api.mdc`](./bookings-api.mdc).
